    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="1211" n="1097" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1097"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> J.C.S. Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United States Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d504-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/> C.C.S. 310</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-15">15 August 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Propaganda Committee</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Recent events have indicated the necessity for establishing some machinery
                    whereby propaganda policies to be followed by London, <pb facs="1212" n="1098"
                        xml:id="pg1098"/> Washington, and Theater Headquarters may be coordinated,
                    particularly in emergency cases.</p>
                <p>The enclosure is presented by the Joint Chiefs of Staff as a possible solution to
                    this problem. They consider it desirable that something along these lines be
                    accomplished during the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quadrant</hi>
                    Conferences.</p>


                <xi:include href="d504-a1.xml" xpointer="d504-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d504-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d504-f1-content">
                <p>For the discussion of this paper at the 116th Meeting of the Combined Chiefs of
                    Staff, August 24, 1943, see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg963">p. 963</ref>.</p>
            </note>
